    "updated_at": "2026-07-17T10:48:52Z",
    "body": "My reading is that _all of the insertion modes are HTML insertion modes_. The [tree construction dispatcher](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#tree-construction-dispatcher) dispatches tokens either to an insertion mode for HTML content _or_ to the rules for parsing tokens in foreign content. Insertion modes and the rules for parsing tokens in foreign content are separate.\n\nThat distinction seems arbitrary; \"foreign content\" seems like another insertion mode on first read. However, making \"foreign content\" another insertion mode would have significant implications. Some examples (not exhaustive):\n\n- [parsing elements that contain only text](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#parsing-elements-that-contain-only-text) captures the original insertion mode, which is later restored.\n- The [rules for parsing tokens in foreign content make use of the current insertion mode](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#parsing-main-inforeign:insertion-mode).\n- The [reset the insertion mode appropriately algorithm](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#reset-the-insertion-mode-appropriately) does not consider foreign content.\n\nIf foreign content were treated as another insertion mode, there would be much more accounting to manage or much heavier reliance on resetting the insertion mode.\n\n---\n\nRegarding the insertion modes, this line is wrong where it mentions CDATA sections:\n\n> The insertion mode affects how tokens are processed and whether CDATA sections are supported.\n\nI opened #12658 to fix it.\n\n---\n\nRegarding the U+0000 NULL handling, there is coverage in WPT primarily via [plain-text-unsafe](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/html/syntax/parsing/resources/plain-text-unsafe.dat). Null in HTML, foreign content, and at integration points seems to have general coverage.\n\nTwo notable coverage gaps:\n- Handling of NULL in MathML foreign content. I only see coverage in SVG foreign content and in MathML at integration points. I don't see tests like `<math>␀` -> `<math>�`.\n- Fragment tests: I haven't noticed tests specifically for fragment parsing with `␀` at different context nodes.\n\nHere's some of the relevant coverage in wpt:\n\n- [`<body>␀`](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/f0b30d60daf6a64a3b087d66732c54c8e5273dbd/html/syntax/parsing/resources/plain-text-unsafe.dat#L76-L89)\n- [`<svg><![CDATA[␀filler␀text␀]]>`](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/f0b30d60daf6a64a3b087d66732c54c8e5273dbd/html/syntax/parsing/resources/plain-text-unsafe.dat#L150-L163)\n- [`<body><svg><foreignObject>␀filler␀text`](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/f0b30d60daf6a64a3b087d66732c54c8e5273dbd/html/syntax/parsing/resources/plain-text-unsafe.dat#L197-L215)\n- [`<svg>␀filler␀text`](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/f0b30d60daf6a64a3b087d66732c54c8e5273dbd/html/syntax/parsing/resources/plain-text-unsafe.dat#L217-L234)\n\n[There also appear to be a number of similar tests for integration points in math.](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/f0b30d60daf6a64a3b087d66732c54c8e5273dbd/html/syntax/parsing/resources/plain-text-unsafe.dat#L436-L518)\n\n(GitHub's web renderer gets confused somewhere in this document; line numbers may be inaccurate either in reality or the rendered view on GitHub)",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
